{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Each case is one evidence set and the grade the matrix must give it. The `must_not_be_proven` cases are the important half: they are the shapes an automated tester mistakes for a finding, and every one of them was an actual mistake somewhere before it was a test case here. The rce cases carrying a reflected token exist because two independent reviewers reproduced the same failure end to end: http.probe writes the caller's token into the evidence record's nonce field, so a parameter that merely reflects it satisfied 'a nonce exists' and the class graded proven with nothing executed.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "rce: nonce echoed with an identity line",
      "vuln_class": "rce",
      "expect": "proven",
      "records": [
        {
          "id": "e1",
          "nonce": "argustest01",
          "command": [
            "id; echo argustest01"
          ],
          "stdout_span": "uid=33(www-data) gid=33(www-data)\nargustest01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "rce: an identity line alone is a real partial signal, and names the two checks it is missing",
      "vuln_class": "rce",
      "expect": "supported",
      "records": [
        {
          "id": "e2",
          "nonce": "argustest02",
          "stdout_span": "uid=0(root) gid=0(root)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "rce: a destructive payload is vetoed, not merely short of a check",
      "vuln_class": "rce",
      "expect": "unproven",
      "records": [
        {
          "id": "e3",
          "nonce": "argustest03",
          "command": [
            "curl",
            "http://t/?c=rm -rf /"
          ],
          "stdout_span": "argustest03"
        }
      ]
    },
